    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bronfman-Building/Experiential-Learning--Partner-Lead_JR0000082501": {
      "title": "Experiential Learning  Partner Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Desautels Position Summary: This position is designed for students who have previously participated as an Experiential Learning (EL) Student Partner. The EL Student Partner Lead will build on their prior experience designing online workshops by supporting the development of new workshop content, leading training workshops, mentoring current EL Student Partners, and contributing to the enhancement and promotion of experiential learning resources. EL Student Partner Lead will: -Assist in the planning, development and delivery of training workshops -Serve as peer mentors for current EL Student Partners throughout the workshop development process, including helping keep EL Student Partners on track and providing feedback -Assist with reviewing and refining existing workshop materials to ensure quality, accessibility, and student engagement -Contribute to the development of new elements of the EL attestation, including the capstone experience and in-person workshops -Attend regular meetings with the project team and participate in feedback and planning discussions Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Previously participated as an EL Student Partner Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to provide thoughtful, constructive feedback to peers Excellent organizational and time-management skills Interest in experiential learning, peer mentorship, and transferable skill development Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment Must be available Fridays from 9:30 to 11:30 between October 23rd and April 2nd, except during Holidays and University Closures Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $24.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 5 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-11-02 Position End Date: 2027-05-28 Deadline to Apply: This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bronfman-Building/Experiential-Learning-Feedback-Coordinator_JR0000082498-1": {
      "title": "Experiential Learning Feedback Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Desautels Position Summary: Experiential Learning (EL) Feedback Coordinators will work together to collect and analyze feedback for the EL Attestation. They will be responsible for developing a feedback strategy, including surveys and focus groups, and executing their strategy. They will analyze the feedback and present their analysis to the EL Attestation Team to guide future content creation and marketing strategy. This is a hybrid position lasting from November 2026 to April 2027. EL Student Partners must be available for weekly check-ins with the EL Team as well as available to attend occasional in-person training sessions on Fridays from 9:30 to 11 am. Beyond these weekly hours, EL Feedback Coordinators should expect to work approximately 3-5 hours per week. EL Feedback Coordinators will: -Meet weekly with the Program leads and occasionally attend the EL Student Partner Friday morning meetings -Develop a coherent and actionable feedback strategy with realistic timeline and clear deliverables -Execute the strategy, including creating and distributing surveys, conducting interviews, organizing focus groups -Analyse the data -Present the analysis in a report and offer suggestions for how to incorporate the feedback Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Current Desautels student (BCom or Masters) Interest in teaching, learning, peer support, or educational content development Interest in data collection, analysis, and/or marketing Ability to analyze both quantitative and qualitative data, r or python skills an asset Strong communication and collaboration skills Ability to work independently and manage project deadlines Experience conducting research a bonus Please submit a CV or Cover letter Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $20.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 3 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-11-02 Position End Date: 2027-05-28 Deadline to Apply: This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bronfman-Building/Experiential-Learning-Student-Partner_JR0000082495": {
      "title": "Experiential Learning Student Partner",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Desautels Position Summary: Experiential Learning (EL) Student Partners will work collaboratively to design and develop engaging online workshops that help students build transferable skills including skills around digital literacy, AI as a learning tool, critical thinking, and other key skills. EL Student Partners will receive training on pedagogy, workshop design, and transferable skills before working in pairs to design and create a workshop of their own. The workshops EL Student Partners create will feature video and voice recordings of the EL Student Partners and will be shared with Bcom students. This is a hybrid position lasting from November 2026 to April 2027. EL Student Partners must be able to attend weekly in-person meetings on Fridays from 9:30 a.m. to 11:00 a.m., during which training will take place, and during which students will record and edit portions of their workshops. Beyond these weekly hours, Student partners should expect to work approximately 3-5 hours per week. EL Student Partners will: -Attend weekly in-person meetings on Fridays from 9:30 a.m. to 11:00 a.m. -Learn the fundamentals of workshop design, learning, and student engagement -Collaborate with a partner to develop an online workshop on a transferable skill -Create workshop materials, including written content, recorded videos, interactive activities, and other learning resources that will be shared with Bcom students -Provide feedback on workshops created by other EL Student Partners Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Current Desautels student (BCom or Masters) Interest in teaching, learning, peer support, or educational content development Strong communication and collaboration skills Ability to work independently and manage project deadlines Interest in AI, digital literacy, critical thinking, or related transferable skills Experience creating digital content is an asset but not required Enthusiasm for helping fellow students learn and develop new skills Please submit a CV or Cover letter. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $20.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 3 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-11-06 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/MacDonald-Harrington/Course-Lecturer---URBP-635-Planning-Law_JR0000082489-1": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer - URBP 635 Planning Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). A comparative study of private and public control of land use and development, including master plans, zoning bylaws, subdivision control, urban redevelopment, expropriation, regional planning, environmental protection, and heritage conservation. Salary: ($11,824) 3 credit course Schedule: Fridays from 8:35 am to 11:25 am Teaching Qualification Requirements: Expertise in content area of the course. Previous experience as an instructor or teaching assistant at the university-level. Evidence of teaching excellence, e.g. McGill COMP Course Evaluations (as Instructor or Assistant). Must have a Law degree. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: School of Urban Planning Course Title: Planning Law Subject Code: URBP 635 Location: Macdonald Harrington Building Schedule: Fridays from 8:35 am to 11:25 am Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-20 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Teaching-Assistant---NEUR-531-503_JR0000082487": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - NEUR 531-503",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Neurology & Neurosurgery Course Title: Computational Neuroscience Course Code: NEUR 531 503 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 45 Hiring Unit: Neurology & Neurosurgery Position Summary: Assist students in computer programming and mathematical analysis related to computational models of brain function. Provide brief instrumental lectures on Matlab and Python programming, Translate assignment code between Python and Matlab. Fourier analysis, differential equations, and linear algebra. Qualifications: Only Current Masters or Doctoral student registered at McGill are eligible to apply as Teaching Assistant, desired major QLS or IPN. Graduate teaching experience is preferred and an asset. Must be eligible to work in Canada. Who are External and Internal Candidates? External Candidates: Current McGill Graduate Student that has held previous jobs/contracts at the university and currently does not have an active job in Workday > applies as an External Candidate  Note: Review the information found here before you apply as an external https://www.mcgill.ca/hr/files/hr/workday_guide_for_applying_to_ta_positions.pdf Internal Candidates: Current McGill Graduate Student with an active job(s)/contract(s) in Workday > applies as an Internal Candidate Before you proceed as an internal candidate, you must log into the VPN before logging into Workday to access the functionality described below. Also, keep in mind that Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) is mandatory for VPN use. Further information regarding 2FA can be found at the following site:   https://www.mcgill.ca/2fa/     Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located.   McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-07 Position End Date: 2027-04-15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
