    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Teaching-Assistant---GPHL-592---W2027_JR0000082461": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - GPHL 592 - W2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Global and Public Health Course Title: Special Topics in Global and Population Health 2 (Women, Health, and Power) Course Code: GPHL 592 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 60 Position Summary: Meet periodically with course supervisors Clarify course content and assignments with students Attend regular Zoom lectures Assist with evaluation/grading Assist with online course management Help prepare and facilitate class discussions, media sharing, and group work Uphold academic integrity and communicate concerns with course supervisors Respond to or share email communications from students with course supervisors as appropriate Qualifications: PhD candidate or 2nd-year Master’s student Organized and efficient with good time management skills Attention to detail regarding all course aspects Approachable and helpful Familiar with course materials and assignments Knowledge of women's health and a strong interest in the topic, reflected in their research or personal engagement Interest in connecting academic research with public and global health an asset Experience in writing, advocacy, or community engagement related to women's health an asset Please note that Teaching Assistants will be required to be on campus to perform their tasks in person. How to Apply To be eligible for a Teaching Assistant position you must be registered at McGill University as a Graduate Student in the term to which you are applying. McGill student not currently employed at McGill University, must apply via external postings. The website will direct you to create a Workday account. Please note, you must use a personal email address when creating this account. Do not use @mail.mcgill.ca or @mcgill.ca email addresses. Candidates who are current McGill employees receiving a salary (not a graduate student stipend) must apply through their already active Workday account. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca or 514-398-3711. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-28 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Winter-2027-TA--NUR1-236-002--003---535-003--NUR-339-005--006_JR0000082333": {
      "title": "Winter 2027 TA: NUR1 236 002, 003 & 535 003, NUR 339 005, 006",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Course Title: Course Code: Estimated Number of Positions: 5 Total Hours of Work per Term: 0 Hiring Unit: Ingram School of Nursing Course Title and Course Number: NUR1 236 002, 003 & 535 003, NUR 339 005, 006 Estimated Number of Positions: 5 Total Hours of Work per Term: 5 x 60   Dates: January 4th - April 30th, 2027 Job Description: The Teaching Assistant (TA) will support the Health and Physical Assessment course for BScN and DE student. This course emphasizes the development of clinical assessment skills and clinical reasoning through lectures, labs, and online activities. The TA will primarily support asynchronous learning and engagement through myCourses. Key responsibilities include: Demonstrates mastery of the course material, including physical assessment techniques, health history taking, and clinical reasoning concepts. Monitors and responds to student questions and group discussions on the  myCourses discussion boards, ensuring timely and accurate responses Responds to general course-related and logistical inquiries via myCourses, McGill email, or other McGill-supported platforms. May contribute to the development and facilitation of  optional recorded review sessions  prior to major evaluations (e.g., midterm and final). Supports faculty with posting announcements to students on myCourses, as needed, to support learning and engagement. Meets with the course instructor(s) at the start and end of term to coordinate expectations, discuss course goals, and review student feedback. Maintains confidentiality and professionalism when accessing course data or gradebooks. May assist in proofreading and formatting evaluation tools (e.g., quizzes or review material) under instructor supervision. Supports the instructional team in maintaining an inclusive, respectful, and collaborative learning environment. Salary: $38.46/hour Desired Major(s): Nursing is mandatory. Desired Degree Level: Masters & Grad Dips & Certs Qualifications: Current Masters or Doctoral student at McGill. Graduate teaching experience is preferred and an asset. Must be eligible to work in Canada McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-14 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-29 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Winter-2027-TA--NUR1-311--Infection-Prevention-and-Control_JR0000082328": {
