    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Teaching-Assistant---BMDE-655---Biomedical-Clinical-Trials--Medical-Devices_JR0000082137": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - BMDE 655 - Biomedical Clinical Trials: Medical Devices",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Biomedical Engineering Course Title: Biomedical Clinical Trials: Medical Devices Course Code: BMDE 655 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Hiring Unit: Biomedical Engineering Course Title and Course Number: BMDE 655 - Biomedical Clinical Trials: Medical Devices Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 hours Job Description Meet with the course instructor, correct and grade quizzes/exams; Provide support and teaching logistics Qualifications: Previously taken the course BMDE655 (preferably) Effective communication skills in English are essential. Only registered graduate students at McGill can be hired as TAs. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-04 Position End Date: 2027-05-07 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-28 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Adams-Building/Research-Assistant-1_JR0000081745": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 1",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Earth and Planetary Sciences Position Summary: Contribute to an ongoing research program focused on the origin and evolution of the Prairie Lake Carbonatite Complex (PLCC), a niobium, phosphate and rare earth elements (REE) deposit. Make observations and collect data leading to a genetic model of the PLCC using established petrographic, mineralogical and geochemical methods Present research findings orally in supervisor meetings, group seminars, and scientific conferences. Support the training and supervision of junior students in the research group.   Qualifications: Prior research experience with limited supervision. Demonstrated ability to independently operate analytical instruments and interpret data used to determine mineral chemical and isotopic compositions. Strong petrographic interpretation skills and demonstrated research problem-solving ability. Strong written and oral communication skills, with the ability to present complex scientific results clearly and effectively. Specialized knowledge of niobium, phosphate and REE mineralogy and mineralization processes, particularly in relation to carbonatite-hosted mineral deposits including SEM, EPMA, LA-ICP-MS and MC-ICP-MS   Experience and Education: BSc in geology, Earth sciences, or a related field Minimum 2 years’ experience in a relevant area of geochemistry acquired through graduate studies or other academic position. Background in metamorphic and metasomatic processes as well as the petrology of silica-undersaturated systems   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 in a scale of 0-4 . Hourly Salary: $30.54 Hours per Week: 16 (Full time) Location: Adams Building Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-02 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-20 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Intramural-Sports-General-Official_JR0000081973": {
      "title": "Intramural Sports General Official",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Athletics & Recreation - Intramural Sports   Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the Intramural Sports General Official will help run the on-going sports programs. Duties include: Officiating intramural matches Game coordination and application of intramural and sports specific rules Assisting with player check-in and scorekeeping Assisting with equipment setup and takedown Maintaining a safe and inclusive playing environment *** Sports Offered: Basketball, Dodgeball, Flag Football, Indoor Cricket, Innertube Waterpolo, Roundnet (Spikeball), Soccer, Ultimate, Volleyball Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Strong knowledge of the selected sport is an asset. Ability to learn quickly and multitask. Well organized with attention to detail. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 1 Year Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE B) $16.85 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 6 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-08-14 Position End Date: 2027-03-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-19 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Faculty-Lecturer_JR0000081188": {
      "title": "Faculty Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\n​ Please refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). The Department of East Asian Studies, Faculty of Arts, McGill University, invites applications for a full-time position of Faculty Lecturer (Contract Academic Staff) in Chinese Language beginning August 1, 2027 and ending July 31, 2030. The appointment may be renewed subject to performance review in the final year.   Minimum qualifications include an MA in linguistics, applied linguistics, Chinese literature, second language education, or a related field. Applicants should have experience teaching Chinese at the college or university level. The successful candidate will be expected to design and teach Chinese language courses across all levels and to engage in pedagogical and curricular innovation in line with the needs of the Department and the University. Candidates should possess native or near-native fluency in Chinese and an excellent command of English. Knowledge of French is an asset.   In addition, all McGill faculty members are expected to contribute to service activities within their units, the University, and the wider scholarly community. A demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion is also expected.   Applicants must complete the online application form. Submission of a letter of introduction, curriculum vitae, and a one-page statement of teaching philosophy is required at the time of application. Short-listed applicants will be invited to submit three reference letters and a teaching portfolio that demonstrates teaching effectiveness (this may include course evaluations from the past five years, sample syllabi, materials related to in-class activities, extracurricular initiatives, and other similar evidence). Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.   Applicants must refer to the McGill Career Site. For Technical guidance, as well as additional instructions on how to submit an application, please refer to the following web-link : https://www.mcgill.ca/hr/files/hr/apply_at_mcgill_university_-_guide_for_external_candidates_en.pdf .   Further inquiries should be addressed to Professor Guojun Wang, Chair of the Search Committee, Department of East Asian Studies, at guojun.wang@mcgill.ca   The deadline for receipt of applications is November 15, 2026 . Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Management-of-Complete-Edentulism-DENT-247_JR0000081894": {
      "title": "Management of Complete Edentulism DENT 247",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Course Title: Management of Complete Edentulism Course Code: DENT 247 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 60 Hiring Unit: Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences Course Title and Course Number: Management of Complete Edentulism DENT 247 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 60 hours Job description:  Teaching and Mentorship - TAs are expected to have a good general knowledge of complete denture prosthodontics and to provide hands-on guidance and supervision to students during laboratory sessions. - TAs will assist students with identification of anatomical landmarks, preliminary impressions, fabrication of custom trays, border molding and final impressions, fabrication and adjustment of record bases, maxillomandibular relationship records, mounting maxillary and mandibular casts on an articulator, artificial tooth set-up and occlusion, and other complete denture laboratory procedures. - TAs will provide technical guidance, troubleshoot laboratory procedures, monitor students’ progress and adherence to instructions, and provide constructive feedback. - TAs will also participate in the evaluation of students’ laboratory work according to the assessment criteria and evaluation sheets provided by the course director.   Qualifications required:   - To hold a DDS, DMD or foreign equivalent. - Be able to perform all techniques required to fabricate complete dentures. - Must be registered in the MSc or PhD program in the field of Dentistry. Name & Title of Course Supervisor: Dr. Carolina B. Meloto Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-05 Position End Date: 2027-06-01 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Teaching-Assistant-DENT-245_JR0000081874": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant DENT 245",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Course Title: Introduction to restorative dentistry Course Code: 245 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 60 Hiring Unit: Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences Course Title and Course Number: Restorative Dentistry DENT 245 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 60 hours Job description:  Teaching and Mentorship - Teach, facilitate and mentor students in learning the basic procedures for fixed prosthodontics in a simulated setting. -Evaluate students’ assignments and provide feedback. -Demonstrate proper technical steps to individual students when required. -Supervise examination sessions.   Qualifications requises / Qualifications required:    DMD from a Faculty of Dentistry. Experience with teaching simulation training for pre-clinical dental students in fixed prosthodontics is considered an asset for this position.   Knowledge and experience with teaching fixed prosthodontic simulation procedures: Tooth preparation for crowns and bridges Temporary crown fabrication with PMMA and Composite Adjustments and cementation of crowns Knowledge on the use of digital scanners is an asset   Name & Title of Course Supervisor: Dr. Samer Abi Nader, Associate Dean UGDE Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-05 Position End Date: 2027-06-03 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, 