    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/5858-Cote-des-Neiges/Teaching-Assistant---FMED-504---Winter-2027_JR0000081929": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - FMED 504 - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Family Medicine Course Title: Family Medicine Research Seminars Course Code: FMED 504 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 20 Hiring Unit: Department of Family Medicine Course Number and Course Title: FMED 504: Family Medicine Research Seminars. Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 20 Position Summary: Assist with course organization and management Assist with online course delivery Assist with student inquiries Assist with assessing student assignments Qualifications: Candidate must be a Ph.D. student in the Family Medicine Program. Application Instructions: Upload your CV with this Workday application. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-04 Position End Date: 2027-03-15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-23 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Brown-Student-Serv/Case-Manager_JR0000081709": {
      "title": "Case Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Student Wellness Hub The Student Wellness Hub provides a range of health services to McGill students with a focus on awareness, prevention, and early intervention. The Student Wellness Hub has a variety of clinicians that provide one-on-one appointments, therapy groups and other services. Within the Student Wellness Hub, the Healthy Living Annex focuses on health promotion and offers peer support programs for both the Macdonald and downtown campuses.  Position Summary: The Case Manager works at the Wellness Hub as part of an interprofessional team supporting student health and wellbeing.   They work from a client-centered approach, integrating culturally relevant practices and perspectives to support the mental health and well-being of students. Working from a stepped care model they connect students to campus and community services that support their mental health needs.   As a Case Manager, their role is to provide students with mental health support and assist with clinical navigation, such as connecting students with complex needs to appropriate levels of support within the Hub, McGill, and the community. Additionally, they collaborate, support, and liaise with professionals at the Hub and members of the community to help ensure that students with complex mental health needs are connected to necessary services. Primary Responsibilities: The primary functions of this position are to provide mental health services directly to students, including those that present in crisis, and to support staff with complex cases. The candidate performs any/all of the following functions as needed: Manage access to care and service navigation for students, clinicians, and staff by facilitating referrals to community-based mental health, medical, and social service providers. Develop and maintain partnerships with community treatment providers, hospitals, intensive outpatient programs, and campus stakeholders to support timely access to appropriate levels of care. Manage urgent, high-risk, and complex cases, serving as the primary contact for safety appointments, crisis consultations, hospitalizations, and transitions between levels of care. Track and monitor priority referrals, hospitalizations, and students of concern, ensuring continuity of care through follow-up, case coordination, and discharge planning. Provide consultation and resource expertise to clinicians, including referral recommendations, care coordination strategies, and assistance navigating community treatment systems. Facilitate communication and information sharing among students, treatment providers, families, faculty, Dean’s Offices, and other stakeholders, including obtaining releases and coordinating treatment records. Maintain and enhance referral resources and systems, including provider databases, referral networks, wait-time information, service availability, insurance coverage, and intake requirements. Deliver training, support strategic initiatives, and collaborate on special projects related to urgent care procedures, hospitalization processes, student support, and campus-wide mental health partnerships.   Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Must be a Master’s-level licensed Mental Health professional within the province of Quebec. Demonstrated ability to make clinical decisions independently. Demonstrated competence working with young adults and able to support students from diverse communities drawing upon personal lived experience. Professionalism, good organizational and interpersonal skills are essential. Must be able to contribute actively to a team.  Excellent presentation and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work in a Microsoft environment using Word, PowerPoint, internet search engines and email. English, spoken and written. French, spoken and read. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 (fluent) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 05) $73,470.00 - $91,840.00 - $110,210.00 Job Profile: MPEX-SAF2B - Student Services - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director Counselling (Case Management) Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-11-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-20 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Brown-Student-Serv/Laboratory-Technician_JR0000081758": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Student Wellness Hub The Student Wellness Hub provides a range of health services to McGill students with a focus on awareness, prevention, and early intervention. The Student Wellness Hub has a variety of clinicians that provide one-on-one appointments, therapy groups and other services. Within the Student Wellness Hub, the Healthy Living Annex focuses on health promotion and offers peer support programs for both the Macdonald and downtown campuses.  Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, participates in the execution of laboratory projects and experiments. Performs a variety of specialized technical tasks according to established methodology. Prepares materials and equipment. Compiles data. Demonstrates techniques. Maintains equipment. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Collects, cleans, and prepares medical equipment/instruments for autoclave sterilization ensuring soiled instruments/equipment are hand washed and sterilized.  Disinfects examination table in all exam & treatment rooms   Ensures consumable items are replenished i.e., latex gloves, PCR swabs, bio-hazard bags, speculums, tissues, masks, etc.   Registers patient specimens, explains laboratory test procedures as required.  Reviews in Medesync for specified results (urgent; + gram stain, + H.Pylori, + STI, etc.) to communicate with medical professionals for review   Assigns results to patient files incorrectly labeled in error  Communicates with immediate supervisor for lab related issues, errors &/or escalation needs.  Communicates via email with hospitals and/or clinics for missing laboratory results  Responds to medical professionals' inquiries related to lab tests/results.   Assist with strep, urine & processes pregnancy tests  Updates Laboratory manuals as required (Sterilization, Main Lab manual, Macdonald, Inventory, etc.) in MS Teams SWH Laboratory Team Group and Confluence  Communicate with FLS, Macdonald Campus, Nurses via MS Teams groups.  Maintains communication within various Teams Groups in MS Teams (SWH Laboratory Team Group, Medical Instruments & Sterilization, Stock Room 4505 Group & Student Wellness Hub Group)  Responsible for maintaining an accurate accounting of all consumables primarily in locked storage rooms.  Responsible for restocking stock room 4505 & treatment room.  Updates inventory Excel spreadsheet after receiving supply shipment in MS Teams SWH Laboratory team Group Inventory   Receives calls & answers general lab inquiries; refers more complex issues to immediate supervisor  Demonstrated ability to explain protocols to patients and obtain informed consent.   The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Demonstrated ability to clearly receive, retain and transmit information with a proven ability to communicate clearly and efficiently at all levels.   Proven ability to be proactive and devote full attention to clientele.  Strong organizational skills with ability to multi-task, prioritize and work under pressure to meet multiple deadlines in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.   Proven discretion in dealing with confidential information.   Must be accurate and possess superior attention to detail with a proven ability to verify work.   Ability to think logically and follow directions. Strong organizational skills and proven ability to multi-task under pressure with strong attention to detail. Knowledge of medical field, an asset. Demonstrated knowledge of the principals of laboratory safety. Demonstrated ability to complete tasks under minimal supervision. Ability to work in a cooperative team environment as well as independently. Proven ability to lift and carry weights of up to 40 pounds, an asset.   Demonstrated ease with technological applications with a proven ability to work in a PC environment using MS Word, Excel, Outlook, MS Teams.   Demonstrated ability to work with clinical and administrative information systems such as Medesync is a very strong asset. English, spoken and written.  French, spoken and read Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 3 (advanced) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III - Medical Laboratory Technology 2 Years Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director Clinical Care Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-12-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-16 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Research-Ethics-Administrator_JR0000081654": {
      "title": "Research Ethics Administrator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: The Research Ethics Administrator (REA) works alongside the Research Ethics Officer throughout the ethics review process of the clinical research. The REA advises researchers and study coordinators on appropriate practices pertaining to clinical research ethics, manages ethics applications to the MUHC Research Ethics Board (REB) and other relevant ethics boards, and ensures administrative and regulatory compliance for clinical research projects. The REA reviews and edits documents, such as informed consent forms, and makes recommendations to sponsors regarding Quebec and Canadian regulatory requirements. The REA also assists with the flow of all documents that require submission to the REB. Primary Responsibilities: Provide effective administrative support for research ethics activities.  Ensure administrative compliance with the practices of McGill University and the McGill University Health Centre, and of industry partners and granting agencies.  Prepare, update, and maintain applicable industry and government regulatory documentation according to Canadian and applicable US standards.  Provide information  to  researchers and study coordinators on the preparation of ethics applications and liaise with sponsors regarding their policies and practices. Respond to inquiries on regulatory agencies' rules and regulations, and University policies and procedures. Implement new policies and new initiatives to support the research program. Keep abreast of regulations and new developments; inform appropriate staff members accordingly. Liaise with the MUHC Research Ethics Board, the MNI Magnetic Resonance Research Committee, researchers, study coordinators, and study sponsors in order to coordinate activities and to ensure that there is adequate communication between all parties.  Keep up-to-date on the Quebec government multicentre mechanism, and communicate with other participating research centres to the extent that it requires. Liaise with sponsors and non-MUHC researchers to initiate clinical trials under the multicentre mechanism.  Interface with the NAGANO research ethics platform. Instruct staff members on the relevant features of the platform.  Help to improve Unit efficiency by recommending changes to the Unit's internal procedures, and implementing decisions made by the CRU's senior management team as they relate to the ethics review process.  Create, prepare, and/or modify consent forms, brochures, and advertising for industry and investigator-initiated research projects.  Prepare and make ethics submissions, including initial applications, amendments, safety reports, and updates. Ensure that safety reports are reviewed and signed by researchers in a timely manner.  Undertake special projects as required. The REA is responsible for the completion of ethics-related projects and tasks that have been delegated to them by the Research Ethics Officer. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Undergraduate degree preferred (B.Sc. or B.A.); Previous research ethics experience and knowledge of the MSSS ethics framework in clinical trials; Knowledge of industry sponsored and grant funded clinical trials an asset; Fully bilingual, English and French; Attention to details and high organizational skills required; Proficient in a PC environment, MS Office; Proven ability to work effectively both independently and in a team-based environment; Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, to carry out multiple projects within the same period, and to adapt and be flexible to changing circumstances; Testing will be administered. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level H) $33.05 - $40.97 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Manager, Operations Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-10-18 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-20 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Brown-Student-Serv/Wellness-Advisor--Athletics---Recreation-_JR0000081795": {
      "title": "Wellness Advisor (Athletics & Recreation)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Student Wellness Hub The Student Wellness Hub provides a range of health services to McGill students with a focus on awareness, prevention, and early intervention. The Student Wellness Hub has a variety of clinicians that provide one-on-one appointments, therapy groups and other services. Within the Student Wellness Hub, the Healthy Living Annex focuses on health promotion and offers peer support programs for both the Macdonald and downtown campuses.  Position Summary: In collaboration with the leadership of faculties & service units, the Wellness Advisor (WA) facilitates the conditions for student well-being where they live & learn. The WA identifies students who may require early intervention & orients them toward the appropriate service, intervention, or care adapted to their situation & reality. The WA will deliver faculty-tailored holistic wellness programming. Primary Responsibilities: Reporting to the Associate Director Wellness (Communities) & housed (embedded) in the partner unit/faculty, the WA:  Acts as liaison between the unit/faculty & Student Wellness Hub as well as other Student Services.  Identifies health promotion & other training needs for the unit/faculty & students. As per the Student Services Collaborative Care (stepped care) model: Delivers wellness workshops & support groups for students; Acts as a consultant to faculty & staff on awareness, prevention, early intervention, & mental health related matters; Conducts relevant trainings for students, faculty, & staff. Conducts initial screening and assessment for students presenting with mental health and wellbeing concerns  Collects and reviews pertinent information/history, drawing on knowledge of mental health and counselling knowledge and skills when making an initial assessment through a structured judgment process.  Determines the need for emergent crisis intervention, facilitates urgent and non-urgent referrals. Initiates the Crisis Management Protocol, if needed. Makes appropriate referrals to a variety of student support services across campus.Maintains up-to-date and comprehensive information on student services and community resources across campus, including faculty-based and central student services (e.g. referral, best practices, policies and processes, etc.) as well as community based mental health services. Acts as a bridge to subsequent care; collaborates with referral sources as needed to streamline students’ access to support, including other mental health care providers, academic advisors, Enrolment Services Professionals, Residence Life Managers, Student Support Services Managers and the Dean of Students. Ensures the support & follow up of referrals. Creates and maintains student records including assessments and referrals as well as appointment information in accordance to established standards, policies and procedures and the Collaborative Care Model. Is a member of the Collaborative Care team in the Student Wellness Hub for the management of students with ongoing (mental) health concerns. Participates in Student Wellness Hub & Student Services meetings & trainings. Encourages & supports institutional policies that address campus wellness & provides strong advocacy for a prevention perspective, principals & values. Promotes to the campus community the linkage between wellness programming & student’s health status, well-being & personal / academic success. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Member of the OCCOQ or other professional order related to field of study, required. Professionalism, good organizational skills with an excellent attention to detail. Demonstrated competence working with young adults.  Proven planning and priority-setting skills. Student-focused and service-oriented with a demonstrated ability to build constructive and effective relationships with all levels of staff, students and the public. Must be self-motivated, empathetic, approachable and self-directed with a demonstrated ability to take responsibility and deliver results with minimum direction and oversight.  Training and experience in mental health assessment of a wide range of concerns that post-secondary student may experience.   Ability to navigate complex student situations, including crisis intervention.  Ability to envision and implement innovative programs and initiatives.  Excellent presentation skills with a  proven ability to communicate, both one-on-one and in a group setting, with tact, diplomacy and sensitivity in a cross-cultural environment to a diverse population.    Able to support students from diverse communities drawing upon personal lived experience, formal training and previous work experience. Lived experience with diverse communities is a strong asset. Demonstrated skills in a PC environment using MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, e-mail and internet search engines.  Demonstrated skills in a PC environment using MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, e-mail and internet search engines. English, spoken and written. French, spoken and read. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 3 (advanced) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here .   As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 05) $73,470.00 - $91,840.00 - $110,210.00 Job Profile: MPEX-SAF2B - Student Services - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director Wellness (Communities) Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-20 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Administrative-Coordinator_JR0000079157": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). *** *** Please note that this is a fully in-office position. Candidates must be available to work from our downtown office five days per week.*** GENERIC SUMMARY: Under the direction of the Director Finance & IT Contracts,  the Administrative Coordinator provides administrative and secretarial support. Participates in ensuring the smooth functioning of IT Services operations. Acts as resource person for policies and procedures. Administers unit accounts. Assists in the organization of unit activities. Responsible for documents and files of the unit. Maintains computerized information systems.   MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide solutions to operational issues within the scope of responsibility by leveraging available resources, reviewing relevant documentation, and liaising with key contacts to obtain and communicate information on diverse and complex topics Communicates with internal and external units/individuals to obtain or supply information. Answers queries related to area of activities. Contribute to the effective operation of IT Services by supporting departmental activities and identifying opportunities for process improvements. Collaborate with the supervisor and team members to establish work priorities, and ensure the timely follow-up and implementation of decisions and initiatives. Administers accounts for unit’s network infrastructure upgrade project. Monitors and reconciles accounts, statements, and reports. Identifies and investigates discrepancies and errors. Makes corrections, processes adjustments and follows up on problems. Audits outstanding items. Compiles information for internal review and analysis by Project Manager and IT Finance Manager.  Ensures information and charges are compliant and within project scope. Coordinates arrangements for events such as workshops. Uses a variety of software. Sets up and maintains databases and spreadsheets of project costs.  Enters data and updates information. Processes purchase orders, travel advances and expense reports. Receive and assist callers and visitors by determining the purpose of their inquiry, preparing necessary documents, and directing them to the appropriate resources to ensure effective service delivery Review and distribute incoming correspondence, prepare files and supporting documentation, and gather information through research as needed. Provide responses to requests within the scope of responsibility, track required actions, and coordinate appropriate follow-up to ensure completion. Arrange meetings and coordinates participant communications and room bookings. Facilitates the organization of events by coordinating logistical requirements and  other arrangements. Maintains office inventory levels and coordinates the procurement of supplies and equipment. Arranges maintenance and servicing of office equipment as required. The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 3 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEP - Secretarial Studies 4 Years Related Experience / DEP - Office Systems Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Supervisor: Manager, Finance & Administration Position End Date (If applicable): 2028-11-05 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEE-273-004-DISE-W27_JR0000081262": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEE 273-004 DISE W27",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDEE 273-004. Elementary School Science 2 Description : Elementary Education : A study of science programs and teaching strategies appropriate for providing elementary school children with an appreciation of the nature and method of science inquiry. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. This course is taught in French. A high level of proficiency in French and ability to teach in French are required. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 360) Schedule:   Friday, 11:35 am-02:25 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education 1.MA in a relevant field (i.e., science education) and/or extensive relevant experience as a school educator/pedagogue/community educator 2.PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset  Experience 1.Expert knowledge of:  Elementary science pedagogy, as outlined in the course description  Research on elementary science pedagogy   Research on elementary students’ scientific thinking and practice  2.Experience as a master teacher/instructor science, mathematics, or a related field in the Quebec educational system  3.Knowledge of the Quebec Education Program (QEP)   4.Familiarity with the professional competencies specified by the Ministère de l’Éducation  Other 1.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the undergraduate level  2.Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion  3.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences   4.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset 5.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools 6.Familiarity of and/or experience with the practice-based pedagigies in science teacher education is an asset. Other information: 1.Commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors. 2.Must be available to attend course coordination meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of course start date. Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Elementary School Science 2 Subject Code: EDEE 273 004 Location: Education Building Schedule: Friday 11:35 am-02:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-28 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDER-372-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081292": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDER 372-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDER 372-001. Culture and Citizenship in Quebec Context (Secondary). Description :Teaching methods and pedagogical resources for programs in ethics and culture in the secondary school. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 431) Schedule: Monday & Wednesday, 02:35 pm-05:25 pm Appointment dates : December 21, 2026 - March 5 , 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1.A Master’s degree (in exceptional circumstances applicants without a Master’s degree but with significant research or professional experience related to the course content may be considered); 2.A teaching degree or equivalent Experience: 1.Expert knowledge of course content and secondary ethics and religious pedagogy; 2.Knowledge of the Quebec Education program (QEP) including ERC program 3.Familiarity with the 13 professional competencies specified by the Ministère de l’Éducation. 4.Experience teaching in the Quebec secondary school system. 5.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) to pre-service teachers. Other: 1.A commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors 2.Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of the course start date Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Culture and Citizenship in Quebec Context (Secondary) Subject Code: EDER 372 001 Location: Education Building Schedule: Monday & Wednesday 02:35 pm-05:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-28 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
