    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Research-Assistant-1_JR0000082761": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 1",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Please fill in the below information as you would like it to appear on the McGill Career Site and delete this line. All other necessary information will appear on the posting automatically and do not need to be included here. If you are not posting the position, this field is not mandatory. Position Summary: The individual will assist in conducting a CIHR-funded longitudinal study examining the progressing of cognitive impairment in individuals with Parkinson’s disease and aimed at identifying the underlying risk and protective factors. We are seeking to fill a position of Research Assistant 1 at the Montreal Neurological Institute under the supervision of Dr. Madeleine Sharp and in consultation with Drs. Alain Dagher and Ron Postuma. The Research Assistant 1 will work under the direct supervision of the principal investigators. The specific responsibilities will include: Implementing established research procedures and protocols Assist with participant recruitment Execute research procedures, including data collection, through interviews, and collection of demographic, clinical, cognitive and MRI data Collaborate with other research teams in implementing established data collection procedures Following data management procedures Compilation of research data and data cleaning Conduct data analysis in support of research activities under supervision Provide guidance to undergraduate and graduate student research assistants in service of the project Perform administrative tasks in relation to the project, e.g. ethics applications The RA 1 will have the opportunity to work with a large number of student and staff researchers as part of this ambitious and collaborative project and will have the opportunity to take part in various educational and research meetings and seminars. There will also be opportunities to contribute to writing research reports. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Subject matter expertise either through Bachelor’s degree or through previous research positions. Minimum of 2 years of relevant work experience. Experience in conducting clinical research is a requirement. Experience with data analysis is also a requirement. Fluency in French and English (spoken and written) as the position will involve regular patient-facing interactions during recruitment and testing. This position is covered by the AMURE Collective Agreement: https://www.mcgill.ca/hr/files/hr/2023-2027_collective_agreement_amure_ras_final_-_with_signatures_-_for_printing_cover_page_reviewed.pdf Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 3 on a scale of 0-4. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $30.54 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Location: Montreal Neuro. Supervisor: Associate Professor (Clinical) Position Start Date: 2026-11-02 Position End Date: 2027-11-01 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-30 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Leacock-Building/Simon---Ethel-Flegg-Postdoctoral-Research-Fellowship--Silver-_JR0000082834": {
      "title": "Simon & Ethel Flegg Postdoctoral Research Fellowship (Silver)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). The Department of Jewish Studies at McGill University invites applications for the Simon and Ethel Flegg Postdoctoral Research Fellowship in Montreal. The one-year postdoctoral fellowship will begin on September 1, 2027. Candidates should specialize in the pre-modern period and complement existing strengths in the department . The department will give special consideration to candidates with a strong emerging record of research and a demonstrated commitment to teaching. Alongside an original research agenda, the Flegg fellow will make an active contribution to Jewish Studies at McGill, including through building intellectual community among faculty and students. The selected candidate must also agree to take up local residence in Montreal during the academic year for the tenure of their fellowship. The Flegg fellow may have the opportunity to teach one undergraduate course as a course lecturer in their area of specialization. Course lecturer contracts are subject to the terms of the MCLIU collective agreement. The fellow will also deliver a public lecture. The annual stipend for the Flegg Postdoctoral Research Fellowship is $58,000 CAD, plus health benefits. Fellows can apply for additional research and travel support. Applicants must have recently been awarded (within 5 years) a PhD or equivalent. The selected candidate must have their PhD in hand by July 1, 2027. Questions about the Flegg Postdoctoral Fellowship should be directed to Professor Ula Madej-Krupitski: ula.madej-krupitski@mcgill.ca . APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Applications must be received through the Workday portal by December 8, 2026 . Applicants should include: 1) a statement of interest detailing the proposed research project; 2) a current curriculum vitae; 4) a copy of the doctoral diploma or a letter from the Department Chair specifying the defense date; 5) a teaching statement with two proposed courses likely to attract a large and diverse group of McGill undergraduate students; 6) a writing sample; 7) full contact information for two individuals who have agreed to write letters supporting your application and who can speak to competence in teaching. Please note that letters of recommendations are only required for shortlisted candidates. Referees will be contacted through Workday and asked to upload their reference letters there. All required documents should be combined into a single PDF file.   LANGUAGE   McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing.  In addition, McGill University is located in the Province of Québec, where the official language is French. As a consequence, existing French language ability, and/or the commitment to attain and maintain French competency, are considered assets.   COMMITMENT TO EQUITY AND DIVERSITY   McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities.   At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry.   McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record.   McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, this email . Annual Salary: $57,557.25 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Location: Leacock Building Supervisor: Associate Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-23 Position End Date: 2028-08-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-12-08 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bronfman-Building/Teaching-Assistant---MGCR-222-ORGB-321_JR0000082652": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - MGCR 222/ORGB 321",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Desautels Course Title: Introduction au comportement organisationnel et au leadership Course Code: MGCR 222 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 57 Position Summary: • updating of course materials • assisting with in-class exam proctoring • supplemental office hours • grading supervision for course midterms and final exam Qualifications: • must understanding basic accounting knowledge • must possess in-depth knowledge of Canadian personal income tax law, including taxation of employment, business, property, and capital incomes Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-03 Position End Date: 2027-04-17 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
