    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-Music/Office-Assistant-A--Manager-Librarian---MUEN-595-001-McGill-Jazz-Orchestra-1_JR0000082115-1": {
      "title": "Office Assistant A (Manager/Librarian - MUEN 595-001 McGill Jazz Orchestra 1",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit Department of Music Performance, Ensemble Resource Office This position is intended for a student with work study eligibility. Main Responsibilities Prepare, distribute and collect sheet music for the ensemble. Submit official attendance records within 24 hours. Efficiently setup and strike all rehearsals in the 30 minutes prior and following rehearsals. Confirm seating charts and assignments for rehearsals. Work directly with the Ensemble Resource Supervisor and Performance Librarian.  The above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks. Required Skills: Good communication in person and via email. Keen attention to detail and timely follow up to emails. Must be a music student. Preference given to member of the ensemble. Work schedule is determined in coordination with the ensemble Director/s according to the needs of the ensemble. May be required to work on weekends. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma Minimal or No Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE A) $16.70 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 1 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-08 Position End Date: 2027-05-01 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-29 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Douglas-Hosp-Burland/Assistant-Professor--Clinical---Department-of-Psychiatry--Geriatric-Psychiatry--C1-261021-_JR0000082787": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Clinical), Department of Psychiatry, Geriatric Psychiatry (C1-261021)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\n​ Please refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Description The McGill University Department of Psychiatry in the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences and the D ouglas Mental Health University Institute are currently inviting applications for a full-time position as a member of the Contract Academic Staff at the rank of Assistant Professor (Clinical). This will be a three-year, renewable appointment and does not confer eligibility for tenure.   The McGill University Department of Psychiatry’s mission is to support patients and their loved ones to move from mental illness to health through cutting-edge integrated care, supported by research and academic training for the next generation. Results of a recent survey of personnel in the department highlighted a collective pride in the excellence of our clinical work, a high degree of satisfaction with teamwork, interdisciplinary collaboration, and a workplace climate that promotes resilience and wellbeing.   Our department has a rich history of scientific innovation with sustained expertise in psychotherapy, substance abuse research, psychoneuroendocrinology, psychoimmunology, genetics, epigenetics, advanced brain imaging, and computational and digital psychiatry. It remains a global leader in integrating cutting-edge science with clinical practice to train future psychiatric researchers and clinicians. We are proud to host a respectful, multi-disciplinary, and inclusive work setting in its multiple areas of activity, which includes the training of a diverse group of students from medicine, psychology, occupational therapy, nursing, and social work.   The Douglas Mental Health University Institute is part of the Montréal West Island Integrated University Health and Social Services Centre, whose mission is to offer cutting-edge care and advance and share knowledge in mental health. The successful candidate will be appointed to clinical practice at the Douglas Mental Health University Institute—a major teaching hospital affiliated with the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences at Canada’s internationally renowned McGill University, located in the vibrant and multicultural city of Montreal, in the province of Quebec.   Job Duties The successful candidate will be expected to carry out clinical activities at the Geriatric Psychiatry Clinic where evaluations and follow-ups of elderly patients are carried out. The successful candidate will be appointed to clinical practice at the Douglas Mental Health University Institute and be expected to contribute to clinical activity in outpatient and inpatient Geriatric Psychiatry. The incumbent will have a broad range of clinical abilities and aptitudes for working in interdisciplinary teams within the Psychiatry program. They will be expected to have a strong academic track record demonstrated by experience in education and/or an active research dossier. In addition to patient care activities, the successful candidate will also be expected to be actively involved in relevant aspects of McGill’s academic mission (e.g., research, teaching, supervision of students and residents, and involvement in academic and administrative committees). All McGill faculty members are also expected to contribute to service activities within their units, the University, and the wider scholarly community. A demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion is also expected.   Qualifications and Education Requirements   Candidates must:   Hold an MD, and hold or be eligible for, licensure as a psychiatrist in the province of Quebec; Have completed advanced Psychiatry training (i.e., fellowship/graduate studies); Possess advanced capacity to engage in all aspects of a university-affiliated psychiatry department (i.e., clinical, education and/or research); Bilingual language skills (French and English) are preferred, or a commitment to acquire the necessary language skills to practice medicine in Quebec. Candidates should be able to interact in English and in French with patients, families, and health care professionals. Assets: Clinician-scientists with MD/PhD (or equivalent research-intensive training) are strongly encouraged to apply; Interest and relevant experience in administration and medical leadership will be considered an asset. undefined Faculty/Department/Unit: Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences, Department of Psychiatry Employee Type: Contract Academic Staff ('Academic Contractual') Rank: Assistant Professor Salary: Remuneration will be according to Quebec health care fee schedule Job Status: Full-time Posting Period: 30 days from date of posting The following supporting documents are required (in one pdf):   ·         Cover letter and curriculum vitae; ·         Statement of Research; ·         Names and contact information of three referees.   Use a personal email address when creating an account in Workday to submit your application. Do not use @mail.mcgill.ca or @mcgill.ca email accounts to apply.   McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing.   L’Université McGill est une institution de langue anglaise dans laquelle la majorité des activités d’enseignement et de recherche s’effectuent en langue anglaise, rendant essentielle l’utilisation de l’anglais pour la communication orale et écrite. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Leacock-Building/Sociology-652-Winter-2027-Teaching-Assistant_JR0000082822": {
      "title": "Sociology 652 Winter 2027 Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Sociology Course Title: Current Sociological Theory Course Code: SOCI 652 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 0 The Department of Sociology is searching for eligible candidates as a Teaching Assistant for the Winter 2027 term. Applicants must be students registered in a McGill MA or PhD graduate program in the Winter 2027 term . ·         Verify Minerva that the Teaching Assistant position for Winter 2027 doesn’t conflict with your own courses. Teaching Assistants will be required on campus to perform their tasks in person and attend all the lectures. Postings are considered tentative pending the final determination of course offerings and enrolments. Due to insufficient enrolment in courses, not all courses posted may require a TA. Position Summary: Responsibilities include hosting and facilitating discussions on Zoom with small groups of students; grading exams and term papers; attending lectures and reading course materials; communicating with students regarding myCourses; submitting assignments, etc.   Qualifications: Position is only available to McGill graduate students with an appropriate academic background. Previous study in the subject of the course.   Position available at 90 hours: SOCI 652 Current Sociological Theory, Peter McMahan (0.5 position)   Hourly Salary: $38.46 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Position Start Date: 2027/01/05 Position End Date:   2027/05/07 Deadline to Apply: 2026/11/04   HOW TO APPLY:   If you have an active job at McGill, you can apply as an INTERNAL APPLICANT : log in and apply through   Workday , using your McGill username and password. IMPORTANT: You MUST first connect to McGill's VPN before you log in to Workday ( instructions on how to download VPN) . If you do not have an active job at McGill, you must apply as an EXTERNAL APPLICANT : navigate to the McGill Career website . First, sign in to your candidate account or create one, as applicable. IMPORTANT: To create your account, make sure to use a personal email address (and NOT an @mail.mcgill.ca or @mcgill.ca email address).     Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-22 Position End Date: 2027-05-07 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-04 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Associate-Director--Financial-Reporting-and-Unrestricted-Accounting_JR0000082782": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Financial Reporting and Unrestricted Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary:   The Associate Director, Financial Reporting and Unrestricted Accounting in the Controller’s Office provides leadership for the University’s accounting and financial reporting activities and supports the integrity, accuracy, and timeliness of the University’s financial information. The role leads the preparation and analysis of key internal and external financial reports, supports the interim and year-end audit processes, oversees the administration and accounting of various University funds, and ensures compliance with applicable accounting standards, legislation, reporting requirements and University policies.   As a leader within the Controller’s Office, the Associate Director translates the Controller’s direction into effective operating practices. The role provides expert accounting and financial analysis, identifies and resolves complex issues, maintains controls current, and leads continuous improvement in financial processes, data and systems.   The Associate Director leads and develops a service-oriented team responsible for financial reporting and accounting, establishing clear priorities and accountabilities while fostering collaboration, professional growth, continuous learning, and effective change adoption.   Primary Responsibilities:   Lead the University's unrestricted accounting and financial reporting, ensuring accuracy, integrity, and compliance with applicable accounting standards and institutional requirements. Oversee the preparation and delivery of quarterly and annual financial statements, government and regulatory reporting, tax filings, and other external financial reporting obligations. Provide expert advice on complex accounting, reporting, and financial matters, including the proactive assessment of financial risks. Monitor financial performance, analyze significant variances and trends, and provide recommendations to support decision-making by senior leadership. Ensure the effectiveness of accounting policies and internal controls in relation with compliance and contribute to the resolution of control issues. Oversee government reporting, reconciliations, and tax-related activities, ensuring compliance with external requirements. Advance the continuous improvement of accounting, reporting, and financial processes, including automation, systems enhancements, data quality improvements, and transformation initiatives. Lead, develop, and manage the team, fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, service excellence, and continuous improvement. Represent the Controller's Office with internal and external stakeholders and exercise delegated financial authorities in accordance with University policies. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Professional accounting designation (CPA) required; CPA Auditor designation or significant external/internal audit experience is an asset. Demonstrates high standards of integrity and professional ethics in all aspects of work. Maintains independence, objectivity, and confidentiality in accordance with applicable professional standards, regulatory requirements, and University policies. Exercises sound judgment, acts with honesty and transparency, and conducts themselves in a manner that supports public confidence in the University's governance and accountability. Strong knowledge of Canadian accounting standards applicable to not-for-profit organizations and demonstrated experience working with auditors, applying accounting standards, financial reporting requirements, and internal controls in a complex organization. Demonstrated progressive experience in financial reporting, accounting operations, audit, compliance, and financial analysis; experience in higher education, the public sector, healthcare, or another highly regulated and complex environment is an asset. Proven people leadership experience, including setting priorities, delegating effectively, coaching and developing staff, managing performance, and leading teams through change. Strong analytical judgment and problem-solving capability, with the ability to assess complex accounting issues, identify financial and control risks, develop options, and translate technical information into clear recommendations. Demonstrated experience improving financial processes, controls, reporting, data quality, and/or financial systems, including successful implementation of change and continuous-improvement initiatives. Advanced proficiency with financial systems, reporting tools, data analysis, and spreadsheet applications; familiarity with McGill financial systems, policies, procedures, and chart of accounts is an asset. English and French, spoken and written. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 5 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 07) $92,150.00 - $115,190.00 - $138,230.00 Job Profile: MPEX-FIN3B - Accounting - Senior Professional/Manager Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Interim Associate Vice-President, Financial Services Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-05 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Royal-Victoria-Coll/Cook_JR0000082798": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: McGill Food & Dining Services  Student Housing & Hospitality Services          Position Summary: Under the direction of the Dining Hall Supervisor, the Chef or the Sous-chef, sees to the preparation, cooking and service of meals.  Qualifications: Diploma from an accredited culinary school plus one (1) year of related experience OR High School Leaving Diploma with five (5) years experience as a Cook.  Ability to read and write English and French.  McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. Good communication skills. Additional Information: Seasonal Position.  Work schedule:  Monday to Friday 8h00-15h45; 38.75hours/week Hourly Salary: $34.42 Hours per Week: 38.75 (Full time) Location: Royal Victoria Coll. Supervisor: Dining Hall Supervisor (ER) Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-05 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
