    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Dental-Hygienist_JR0000081006": {
      "title": "Dental Hygienist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). GENERIC SUMMARY: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, perform dental imaging procedures, including intraoral radiography, panoramic imaging, cephalometric imaging, and cone beam computed tomography (CBCT). Ensure the production of high-quality diagnostic images and adherence to radiation safety and infection control standards. Support daily clinical operations through equipment maintenance, digital image management, quality assurance activities, and collaboration with clinical instructors and staff. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: (i) Demonstrate various techniques for obtaining intraoral radiographs on manikins and patients. (ii) Provides instruction and technical assistance to dental students during radiographic procedures (iii) Monitors radiographs taken by students to assess technical quality and determine whether images are diagnostically acceptable. (iv) Performs intraoral, panoramic, cephalometric, and CBCT imaging procedures on patients according to established protocols. (v) Instructs students on panoramic radiographic techniques, including patient positioning and image acquisition procedures. (vi) Communicates radiographic concerns and errors to the unit Head to ensure appropriate follow-up and improvement. (vii) Ensures radiographic procedures are performed safely and efficiently while following radiation protection principles. (viii) Organizes and transfers radiographic images received electronically from external sources into appropriate patient records. (ix) Communicates with image senders when clarification, additional information, or follow-up is required. (x) Prepares and distributes radiographic images electronically or on digital media (e.g., CDs) for referrals, consultations, specialist treatment, and insurance approval purposes. (xi) Performs routine monitoring, maintenance, and basic troubleshooting of dental radiology equipment and imaging systems. (xii) Communicates equipment issues, including sensor or imaging system concerns, to the Clinic Manager and coordinates follow-up when required. (xiii) Ensures radiology rooms are clean, organized, and compliant with infection prevention and control standards. (xiv) Prepares radiology rooms and maintains availability of required supplies, instruments, and protective materials. (xv) The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks, which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: -- DCS Diagnostic Imaging Technology -- 2 years of related experience As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 3(qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III - Dental Hygiene 2 Years Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level G) $31.19 - $38.65 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Administration Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-10-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-13 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
