    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Mtl-General-Hosp/Research-Assistant-1_JR0000082618": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 1",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Registered Dietitian supporting perioperative nutrition and prehabilitation research through nutrition assessment, individualized counselling, participant monitoring, and delivery of study interventions according to research protocols. Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree required.  Registered Dietitian. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $30.54 Hours per Week: 3 (Part time) Location: Mtl. General Hosp. Supervisor: Assistant Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-19 Position End Date: 2027-10-29 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-28 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Meredith-LadyHouse/Student-Research-Assistant_JR0000082743-1": {
      "title": "Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Institute of Health Sciences Education Position Summary: Seeking a research assistant to help with coordination and administration for two studies in health professions education. Tasks will include meeting with the research team on a regular basis, facilitating study coordination in including participant recruitment and scheduling, coordinating and assisting in data collection as needed, participating in descriptive analysis as needed, ensuring rigorous research practices, and assisting in the final grant report and knowledge dissemination products. Project management Study coordination and project administration Qualifications:   Must be a registered graduate student at McGill University and living in Quebec Must have experience with coordinating and leading the administration of research studies Must have experience in descriptive data analysis Must have familiarity with the complexities of launching and running multiple research projects Experience working in interdisciplinary research teams At minimum MA/MSc level training Accuracy and attention to detail Sense of motivation and ability to work independently Willingness and ability to work flexible hours Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4. Hourly Salary: $32.00 Hours per Week: 5 (Part time) Location: Meredith, Lady,House Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-21 Position End Date: 2027-02-01 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-29 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McLennan-Library/Class-Scheduling-Administrator_JR0000082679": {
      "title": "Class Scheduling Administrator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Reporting to the Class Scheduling Manager, the Class Scheduling Administrator is responsible for gathering the information required for scheduling, assessing, and updating the information in the scheduling software. The incumbent represents the Class Scheduling Team as a resource person and trouble-shooter for University staff and faculty, while assessing, reviewing, and investigating record discrepancies and producing scheduling timetables for departments.  Primary Responsibilities: Produce a timely, accurate, and conflict-free schedule for students and Faculty by collecting and validating data submitted by academic departments and producing schedules in a timetable software. Responsible for preparing and publishing the class schedule prior to Registration. Evaluate and manage scheduling constraints to minimize conflicts, maximize efficiency, and develop optimal schedules. Ensure the schedule meets the effective delivery of the program. Ensure that the timetable provides effective space utilization. Monitor class scheduling data to improve data quality, resolve issues, and review unused space. Monitor and adjust schedules before and during the academic year to reflect enrolment changes and department requests.  Conduct  testing of system software upgrades and any additional testing required to support scheduling-related projects. Train departments on the use of the Data Collection Utility (DCU) and provide accurate information to the scheduling team. Responsible for updating Class Schedule documentation and completing ad-hoc requests for events or exams, as required. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities  : Proven ability to handle several operational deliverables simultaneously, meet deadlines and work independently, as well as part of a team. Demonstrated organizational skills, ability to prioritize and multi task.  Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with all levels of staff. Ability to identify and solve problems using initiative and creativity. Ability to analyze processes and procedures and to advise on improvements. Ability to work unsupervised and independently to meet deadlines, planning, and setting priorities for own work. Ability to priorities multiple tasks, work to resolve conflicting timelines, and deadlines under pressure and make informed decisions with limited supervision. Ability to work efficiently integrating new knowledge and process improvement. Demonstrated commitment to client focused service with an ability to interact effectively with a wide variety of individuals, including all members the over-arching Systems, Projects, and Class Scheduling team using well developed interpersonal and negotiation skills. Ability to communicate complex information effectively and professionally to a range of customers with varying levels of understanding. Strong commitment to collaborate and work together as a team to produce an effective schedule within the established timeline. Knowledge in PC environment using word processing, databases, spreadsheets, power point, Banner and TPHI. Interpersonal skills using tact, patience and courtesy.  Please note that the recruitment process for this position may include a testing component following the interview.  As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #3 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience with DEC III / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level H) $33.05 - $40.97 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Class Scheduling Manager Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-07-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-30 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bishop-Mountain-Hall/General-Helper-A--Casual-_JR0000079612": {
      "title": "General Helper A (Casual)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Student Housing & Hospitality Services Under the direction of the Supervisor, Dining Hall or Chef, performs tasks required to maintain the cleanliness of cooking utensils and equipment and the kitchen area.   Qualifications Required - High School Leaving Diploma.  - Three (3) months related experience.  - Good communication skills.  - Ability to communicate, read and write English and French.  Knowledge of French and English. McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. Additional Information Temporary part-time position for the period August 22, 2026 to April 30, 2027. Work hours and location are variable. Hourly salary: $24.40/hour Hours of work: up to 38.75 per week (day, evening, night). Must be available for weekend schedules from Sunday to Saturday, according to needs. Location: Bishop Mountain Hall/Royal Victoria College/Douglas Hall, as per need. Supervisor: Dining Hall Supervisor and/or Chef As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy (if eligible) Two (2) personal days (if eligible) Two (2) floating holidays (if eligible) Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day (if eligible) Paid time off over the December holiday period (if eligible) Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits (if eligible) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
