    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Morrice-Hall/Graduate-Student-Copy-Editor_JR0000082741": {
      "title": "Graduate Student Copy Editor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). *** This position is exclusively available to McGill graduate students. ***   Hiring Unit: McGill University Libraries Supervisors : Co-editors of the volume, Katherine Hanz, Associate Dean, User Services, and Anaïs Salamon, Head, Islamic Studies Library Hours of work : 12 to 15 hours a week for a max of 300 hours. Duration: unit March 13, 2027 with ^possibility of extension. Hourly Rate: $22.10   Background & Position Summary: The McGill Libraries are currently working towards the publication of the Fourth Abu Dhabi International Manuscripts Conference held in Abu Dhabi on October 8 and 9, 2025. This conference was co-organized by the McGill Libraries and the Department of Culture and Tourism in Abu Dhabi within the frame of a broader collaboration involving the curation of a manuscript's exhibition entitled Golden Ink displayed in Abu Dhabi in the Fall 2025-Winter 2026 and to be displayed in Montreal in 2028, and the publication of an exhibition catalogue . For the Proceedings, we are seeking a skilled Copyeditor / Proofreader to review fourteen papers in English and Arabic. Under the direct supervision of the co-editors, the student will be responsible for checking spelling and grammar errors, check formatting for compliance with author’s guidelines, review citations formatting, etc.   Description: Check and correct spelling and grammar errors Check formatting to ensure it complies with the author’s guidelines Check citations to ensure accuracy and consistency with APA Communicate with the editor Assign titles, subtitles Integrate images, figures and illustrations within the text   Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: High attention to detail Fluency and excellent written skills in English and Arabic Strong computer/technological skills (Word, Acrobat, etc). Strong editorial skills Proficiency with citations formatting Good communication skills Demonstrated organizational skills, and ability to work independently English: spoken, read and written. French: read.   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 3 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 1 Year Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE B) $22.10 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 12 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-21 Position End Date: 2026-12-23 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-06 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Teaching-Assistant-EDKP-394-KPE-W27_JR0000082557": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant EDKP 394 KPE W27",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Kinesiology and Physical Education Course Title: Historical Perspectives Course Code: EDKP 394 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 65 This posting is for one unionized contractual appointments. A Teaching Assistant is a Graduate Student employed to assist the Course Supervisor as a Teaching Assistant in a classroom environment. Teaching Assistant Positions are governed by the Collective Agreement between McGill University and the Association of Graduate Students Employed at McGill (AGSEM) . Hiring Unit: Department Kinesiology and Physical Education Course Title and Course Number: EDKP394 Historical Perspectives Name & Title of Course Supervisor: Jordan Koch, Associate Professor Position Summary: This requisition is for one position, at 65 hours for the term, in the Department Kinesiology and Physical Education . Course dates are January 5, 2027 to April 14, 2027. Effective dates of appointment are December 28, 2026 to April 30, 2027. Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 65 hours Hourly Rate: $38.46/hr Required Duties: Assist students with their group virtual projects and presentations Prepare question/answer content from labs for MyCourse quizzes Prepare and assist with Midterm and final exam Communicate with graders to clarify question/answer keys Qualifications: Must be a graduate (master’s or PhD) student enrolled at McGill University, ideally the Kinesiology and Physical Education program. Background in the humanities (history, sociology, anthropology) also desirable;  Strong writing and oral communication skills; Attention to detail & accuracy; Familiarity with course content. English, spoken and written. French, spoken and written, is an asset Application Deadline: Applicants have until November 2, 2026 (11:59PM) to apply for this posting. McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-12-28 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
