    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Teaching-Assistant-EDKP-495-KPE-W27_JR0000082571": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant EDKP 495 KPE W27",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Kinesiology and Physical Education Course Title: Scientific Principles of Training Course Code: EDKP 495 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 50 This posting is for two unionized contractual appointments. A Teaching Assistant is a Graduate Student employed to assist the Course Supervisor as a Teaching Assistant in a classroom environment. Teaching Assistant Positions are governed by the Collective Agreement between McGill University and the Association of Graduate Students Employed at McGill (AGSEM). Hiring Unit: Department Kinesiology and Physical Education Course Title and Course Number: EDKP 495 Scientiﬁc Principles of Training Name & Title of Course Supervisor: Dennis Jensen, Associate Professor Estimated Number of Positions: 2 positions Total Hours of Work per Term: 50 Hours each (Total 100 hours) Hourly Rate: $38.46/hr Position Summary: Required Duties : Assist instructor with (1) proctoring and marking of midterm and final exams; (2) marking assignments; and (3) holding office hours (either in-person or virtual) to address student questions/concerns about exams, assignments and perhaps also course material. Qualifications: BSc in Kinesiology or related field, with evidence of classroom, research (laboratory), and/or professional experience in clinical exercise physiology (EDKP 485) or scientific principles of training (EDKP 495). Language Requirements: Fluency in English is required.  Fluency in French is a benefit, but not required Application Deadline: Applicants have until November 2, 2026 (11:59PM) to apply for this posting. McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-12-28 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
