    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Casual-Research-Assistant-1_JR0000082615-1": {
      "title": "Casual Research Assistant 1",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Ingram School of Nursing Position Summary: Literature Review & Background Research Search, collect, and summarize relevant academic or clinical literature to support research questions and project development.   Data Collection Conduct surveys or interviews; gather quantitative and qualitative data following ethical protocol.   Data Management Enter, clean, code, and organize data using tools such as Excel, SPSS, NVivo, or other software.   Data Analysis Assist in running statistical tests, thematic analysis, or other methods under supervision of the researchers.   Documentation Keep detailed notes of procedures, research protocols, and results to ensure accuracy and reproducibility.   Report Writing & Dissemination Draft sections of research papers, abstracts, presentations, or posters; format references; prepare materials for conferences or publications.   Administrative Support Coordinate research logistics such as scheduling meetings, maintaining databases, filing ethics documentation, and handling correspondence with participants.   Qualifications: Knowledge in related field Bilingual French and English Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 on a scale of 0-4. Hourly Salary: $30.54 Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Location: Various Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-19 Position End Date: 2026-12-15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-27 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bronfman-Building/Teaching-Assistant---MGCR-222_JR0000082690": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - MGCR 222",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Desautels Course Title: Introduction au comportement organisationnel Course Code: MGCR 222 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Hiring Unit: Desautels Faculty of Management Course Title and Course Number: Introduction to Organizational Behaviour MGCR 222 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Position Summary: 1) assignment preparation and grading 2) course attendance & office hours 3) preparation and grading for the midterm exam and the final exam Qualifications: Must be McGill graduate student with appropriate course background Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-03 Position End Date: 2027-04-17 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/St-Marys-Hospital/Assistant-Professor--Clinical---Department-of-Pediatrics--C3-261008-_JR0000082496": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Clinical), Department of Pediatrics (C3-261008)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\n​ Please refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Description The McGill University Department of Pediatrics in the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time position at the rank of Assistant Professor (Clinical) based at the St. Mary’s Hospital Centre. This will be a three-year, renewable Contract Academic Staff appointment and does not confer eligibility for tenure.   The Department of Pediatrics is a leader in academic medicine. Our educational and research missions support excellent and innovative clinical programs across our teaching hospitals.  At St. Mary's Hospital Center in Montreal, the intermediate care neonatology nursery provides Level IIA (Level 2a) neonatal care services. This specialized nursery is designed for close medical monitoring of newborns who require extra supervision but do not need full tertiary critical care or intensive care.   The St. Mary's Hospital Center (SMH) is a teaching hospital affiliated with the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences at Canada’s internationally renowned McGill University, located in the vibrant and multicultural city of Montreal, in the province of Quebec. As a key academic healthcare institution, the SMH is dedicated to excellence in patient care, education, and research. Situated in Montreal's vibrant West Island region, the hospital offers a dynamic environment for clinical practice and medical training.   Job Duties The successful candidate will join the Department of Pediatrics and will provide care primarily for healthy newborns, working alongside a skilled team of obstetricians, nurses, and allied health professionals. The successful candidate will also be a clinical leader in managing infants who require additional support, from delivery room resuscitation to stabilization and transfer to tertiary care when necessary. For infants with complex conditions or requiring subspecialty input, we benefit from excellent collaboration with tertiary centers, particularly the Montreal Children’s Hospital and the Jewish General Hospital. The successful candidate will be expected to: Provide comprehensive care to newborns in a Level 2A nursery. Collaborate closely with obstetrical, nursing, and allied healthcare professionals to ensure the delivery of high-quality, patient-centered care. Participate in a shared on-call schedule averaging 6-7 shifts per month, including daytime hospital coverage and overnight telephone coverage from home, with the ability to return to the hospital when required for emergencies. Conduct outpatient follow-up assessments for newborns during their first week of life. Respond promptly to neonatal and newborn-related emergencies within the hospital setting. Provide occasional clinical coverage at affiliated network hospitals, including Lakeshore General Hospital and LaSalle Hospital, to support continuity of care across the Montreal West Island Integrated University Health and Social Services Centre network. The successful candidate is expected to perform clinical duties and attend departmental and division meetings. The successful candidate will also be expected to be actively involved in relevant aspects of McGill’s academic mission (e.g., research, teaching, supervision of students and residents, and involvement in academic and administrative committees).   McGill faculty members are expected to contribute to service activities within their units, the University, and the wider scholarly community. A demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion is also expected.   Qualifications and Education Requirements   Candidates must:   Hold an MD degree (or equivalent), or be eligible for, licensure in the province of Quebec; Have completed training in Pediatrics and be eligible for competency-based certification by the Collège des médecins du Québec or the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada (or equivalent); Special interest in breastfeeding, with a commitment to supporting breastfeeding mothers and promoting lactation support within the hospital setting. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with an emphasis on family-centered care. Bilingual language skills (French and English) are preferred, or a commitment to acquire the necessary language skills to practice medicine in Quebec. Candidates should be able to interact in English and in French with patients, families, and health care professionals.   Faculty/Department/Unit: Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences, Department of Pediatrics, St. Mary’s Hospital Employee Type: Contract Academic Staff ('Academic Contractual') Rank: Assistant Professor Salary: Remuneration will be according to Quebec health care fee schedule Job Status: Full-time Posting Period: 30 days from date of posting The following supporting documents are required:   ·       Cover letter and curriculum vitae; ·       Statement of research; ·       Names and contact information of three referees.   Use a personal email address when creating an account in Workday to submit your application. Do not use @mail.mcgill.ca or @mcgill.ca email accounts to apply.   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing.   L’Université McGill est une institution de langue anglaise dans laquelle la majorité des activités d’enseignement et de recherche s’effectuent en langue anglaise, rendant essentielle l’utilisation de l’anglais pour la communication orale et écrite. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Burnside-Hall/Teaching-Assistant---MATH-463-563--W27-_JR0000082683": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - MATH 463/563 (W27)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Mathematics and Statistics Course Title: Convex Optimization Course Code: MATH 463 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 45 Hiring Unit: Mathematics and Statistics Course Title and Course Number: Convex Optimization / Honours Convex Optomization - MATH 463/563 (Winter 2027 Jan to April) Total Hours of Work per Term: 45 Hours Position Summary: *NOTE: Please apply through the Careers website as an \"External Candidate\". Use your legal name, a Canadian home address, and a personal email address when creating your external applicant profile (do not use your McGill email). International candidates must have a Canadian bank account, valid SIN and study permit.* Each Teaching Assistant will be responsible for a tutorial group. This will entail: Giving tutorials. These involve the formal presentation of carefully prepared illustrative examples worked at the blackboard. Students should be given ample chance to ask questions. Some time may be spent on more informal classroom activities - helping individual students as they work individually or in groups. At least two regularly scheduled office hours per week - the times to be announced at the first tutorial. Marking of assignments of the tutorial group. Invigilation of the midterm at the scheduled time. Team marking of the midterm and final examination under the close supervision of the Faculty teaching the course (who will also set the examinations). Final examinations must NEVER be handed back to students. Maintenance of the complete mark record for the tutorial group. A teaching assistant may be assigned a coordinating or supervisory role in the marking process. Teaching assistants may also be asked to cooperate in preparing solution sheets to assignments. They may be asked to set and mark occasional short \"surprise tests\" which can be used to encourage regular attendance. Maintaining the online platform: read posts from students and write responses. Qualifications: Must be a McGill graduate student Honours Degree in Mathematics, Statistics or Applied Mathematics, with high standing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-20 Position End Date: 2027-04-10 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-27 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/JGH---Jewish-General-Hosp/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor--Clinical---Department-of-Obstetrics-and-Gynecology--Two-Positions--C4-261008-and-C5-261008-_JR0000082631": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor (Clinical), Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Two Positions (C4-261008 and C5-261008)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\n​ Please refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Description The McGill University Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology in the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences invites applications for two full-time Contract Academic Staff positions at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor (Clinical) based at the Jewish General Hospital (JGH). The professorial rank of the two successful candidates will be determined according to the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. This will be a three-year, renewable appointments and does not confer eligibility for tenure.   The OBGYN Department at the Jewish General Hospital comprises specialists and subspecialists who provide the full complement of Obstetrical, Gynecologic and Oncologic services to the population. Our department is made up of 6 general OBGYN’s, 7 MFMs, 4 MIS and 5 Gyn Oncologist subspecialists. The JGH is the busiest Obstetrical centre on the island of Montreal, and our group ensures 24/7 in-house coverage of our high-volume labour and delivery unit, doing approximately 3600 deliveries per year. We collaborate with and support our Family Medicine Obstetrical Team and Midwifery team. We are a Tertiary level Centre offering specialized MFM care for complex pregnancy related conditions, and we receive many high-risk transfers from across the province annually. Our division of MIS ensures care of several thousand patients with complex gynecological cases and performs over 1000 surgical procedures per year using multiple approaches. Our Gyne-Oncology division provides state-of-the-art care to thousands of patients with gynecological malignancies and performed almost 300 robotic surgical cases last year. These two positions will be based at the Jewish General Hospital—a major teaching hospital affiliated with the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences at Canada’s internationally renowned McGill University, located in the vibrant and multicultural city of Montreal, in the province of Quebec.   Job Duties The two successful candidates will be members of the Department of OBGYN at the Jewish General Hospital. They are expected to perform clinical duties and attend the majority of department meetings and rounds, as well as provide excellent clinical teaching and supervision to undergraduate medical students, OBGYN residents, Family medicine residents and Fellows. The successful candidates are expected to take a normal allotment of Obstetrical call and bring an average volume of obstetrical patients to the institution, approximately 150 or more per year. The incumbents will be expected to take some MIS call as well.   The incumbents will also be expected to be actively involved in relevant aspects of McGill’s academic mission (e.g., research, teaching, supervision of students and residents, and involvement in academic and administrative committees).   McGill faculty members are expected to contribute to service activities within their units, the University and the wider scholarly community. A demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion is also expected.   Qualifications and Education Requirements   Candidates must:   Hold an MD degree (or equivalent), and be eligible for, licensure in the province of Quebec; Have completed a minimum 1-year fellowship specialty training in Obstetrics and Gynecology and be eligible for competency-based certification by the Collège des médecins du Québec or the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada (or equivalent); Hold a Master’s degree or other postgraduate training (preferred, not required); Bilingual language skills (French and English) are preferred, or a commitment to acquire the necessary language skills at the level needed to practice medicine in Quebec. Candidates should be able to interact in English and in French with patients, families, and health care professionals.   Faculty/Department/Unit: Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences, Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Jewish General  Hospital Employee Type: Contract Academic Staff ('Academic Contractual') Rank: Assistant/Associate Professor Salary: Remuneration will be according to Quebec health care fee schedule Job Status: Full-time Posting Period: 30 days from date of posting Number of positions: 2 The following supporting documents are required:   ·         Cover letter and curriculum vitae; ·         Statement of Research; ·         Names and contact information of three referees.   Use a personal email address when creating an account in Workday to submit your application. Do not use @mail.mcgill.ca or @mcgill.ca email accounts to apply.   McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. L’Université McGill est une institution de langue anglaise dans laquelle la majorité des activités d’enseignement et de recherche s’effectuent en langue anglaise, rendant essentielle l’utilisation de l’anglais pour la communication orale et écrite.   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Office-Assistant-C_JR0000082674-1": {
      "title": "Office Assistant C",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Job Description   Provides advanced administrative support to the Office of First Nations and Inuit Education (OFNIE), with a focus on course administration, student registration, instructor support, records management, and day-to-day operational coordination.   Primary Responsibilities Support course administration and student registration processes. Prepare, maintain, and organize student, instructor, and course records. Prepare course packages, instructional materials, and other administrative documentation. Track attendance, course completion, and end-of-course documentation. Monitor outstanding administrative requirements and ensure timely follow-up. Provide administrative support to instructors throughout the course delivery process. Coordinate administrative follow-up with students, instructors, Indigenous education partners, and relevant University units. Respond to routine inquiries and direct more complex matters to the appropriate individuals or departments. Coordinate the preparation, distribution, shipment, and tracking of course materials and documentation. Maintain tracking tools and follow up on outstanding materials or administrative requirements. Ensure course materials and related documentation are organized and available as required. Assist with the organization and coordination of meetings, events, and other OFNIE activities. Schedule meetings, prepare invitations and participant lists, and coordinate logistical arrangements. Prepare meeting materials and maintain related records and follow-up documentation. Prepare and maintain spreadsheets, tracking tools, reports, lists, and electronic files to support OFNIE operations. Ensure the accuracy, completeness, organization, and confidentiality of administrative records. Maintain up-to-date documentation to support course delivery, student administration, and operational requirements. Manage multiple priorities and deadlines while ensuring the timely completion of assigned tasks. Exercise sound judgment and initiative in resolving routine and more complex administrative matters. Work independently while collaborating closely with the OFNIE administrative team. Perform other related administrative duties as assigned.   Qualifying Skills and Abilities Strong organizational, time-management, and follow-up skills, with attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, work independently and collaboratively, and exercise sound judgment. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams); familiarity with SharePoint and electronic file management is an asset. Ability to maintain accurate records, prepare spreadsheets and reports, and learn new administrative systems and processes. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and communicate professionally with diverse stakeholders. Fluency in English; French is an asset. Interest in Indigenous education and community-based programs; experience in academic or student administration is an asset. Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $29.42 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-20 Position End Date: 2027-04-19 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-26 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Hosmer-House/Teaching-Assistant--Winter-2027--Community-Based-OT--OCC1-622-_JR0000082670": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant- Winter 2027- Community-Based OT (OCC1 622)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: School of Physical and Occupational Therapy Course Title: Community-Based OT Course Code: OCC1 622 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Job Description: The Teaching Assistant (TA) will assist with the preparation of course material, managing myCourses, leading discussions, answering student inquiries, grading and providing feedback on student work. The TA will also support some in-class sessions and assess students' work related to course objectives.   Desired Major(s): Occupational Therapy Desired Degree Level: Masters & Grad Dips & Certs Qualifications:   Current Masters or Doctoral student at McGill.   Graduate teaching experience is preferred and an asset.   Must be eligible to work in Canada     *Previous experience with teaching or TA in OCC1-443 required.   *Clinical experience as occupational therapist working in psychosocial rehabilitation and/or with marginalized populations and/or community-based practice required.     McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment.   Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-03-08 Position End Date: 2027-05-11 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Hosmer-House/Teaching-Assistant--Winter-2027--Measurement-in-Rehabilitation-1--POTH-620-_JR0000082494": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant- Winter 2027- Measurement in Rehabilitation 1 (POTH 620)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: School of Physical and Occupational Therapy Course Title: Measurement in Rehabilitation 1 Course Code: POTH 620 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Job Description: The course will be focused on biomechanics and measurement theory.  Students will have to use Matlab to process and analyze biomechanical data. Under the supervision and in collaboration with the course coordinators, TAs will assist students with labs/practical components of the course. TAs will also be responsible for grading lab assignments and presentations. The TA is expected to attend all labs and must therefore be available at the scheduled class time. Desired Major(s): Physical Therapy, Occupational Therapy, Kinesiology, Engineering  Desired Degree Level: Masters & Grad Dips & Certs  Completed BSc previously. Current MSc or PhD student.  Qualifications: Current Masters or Doctoral student at McGill.  Graduate teaching experience is preferred and an asset.  Must be eligible to work in Canada  The candidate must have completed graduate courses in biomechanics. Having previously completed POTH 620 will be an asset. Candidates should be intermediate or advanced users of Matlab.   The candidate must have previously completed a course in biomechanics and has experience conducting biomechanics research, preferably in the areas of motion capture, dynamometry, electromyography.   McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment.   Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Hosmer-House/Teaching-Assistant--Winter-2027--Introduction-to-Professional-Practice-II--POTH-250-_JR0000082502": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant- Winter 2027- Introduction to Professional Practice II (POTH 250)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: School of Physical and Occupational Therapy Course Title: Introduction to Professional Practice II Course Code: POTH 250 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Job Description: Teaching Assistants (TAs) for POTH-250 will support various instructional and evaluative activities throughout the course. Specific responsibilities will be determined collaboratively between the course coordinators and the TAs. Tasks may include, but are not limited to, the following:    Facilitating small group learning during simulation activities  Assisting in therapeutic massage laboratory sessions  Evaluating student performance during Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs)  Grading written student assignments  Providing constructive feedback on student submissions  Attending or reviewing selected lectures to prepare for grading or assisting in hands-on workshops  Reviewing course materials to support grading and workshop facilitation  Utilizing the MyCourses platform for course-related tasks Desired Major(s):    Ideally, Teaching Assistants will have a clinical background in:     Physical Therapy   Occupational Therapy   Other healthcare discipline    Desired Degree Level:    Masters and/or PhD students    Qualifications:   Current Masters or Doctoral student at McGill.  Graduate teaching experience is preferred and an asset.  Must be eligible to work in Canada  McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-01 Position End Date: 2027-05-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
