    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Senior-Functional-Business-Analyst_JR0000082880-1": {
      "title": "Senior Functional Business Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Context: The Senior Functional Business Analyst will be fully dedicated to the University's ERP Modernization Program, with a focus on the Student Information Systems (SIS) project. This transformational initiative aims to modernize the technology, processes, and services that support the student lifecycle. The University's current ERP system, Ellucian Banner, has been in place for many years and includes significant customization. As a result, many business processes and rules have evolved around the system and may no longer reflect current business needs. The Senior Functional Business Analyst will work closely with stakeholders to understand existing processes, identify underlying requirements, and distinguish business-driven needs from legacy practices. Working in partnership with Functional Analysts (FAs) and technical teams, the Senior Functional Business Analyst will develop a deep functional and hands on knowledge of Banner, including system configuration business rules, workflows and functional dependencies. The Senior Functional Business Analyst will actively participate in solution design, configuration, validation and troubleshooting, and will progressively develop the expertise required to support long-term functional ownership of the solution. This role requires an experienced professional with strong business analysis capabilities who can bridge business needs, operational processes and system functionality, understand cross-functional impacts, facilitate decision-making, and support stakeholders through organizational change. The Senior Functional Business Analyst will remain engaged throughout the project lifecycle, from business analysis and process design through solution development, testing, implementation, and business acceptance, ensuring that solutions meet intended business outcomes. The Senior Functional Business Analyst will combine strong business analysis capabilities with hands-on functional expertise, translating business needs into practical system solutions and helping ensure that business processes and system configuration remain aligned. Main Responsibilities: Develop a strong understanding of current student administration processes and the Ellucian Banner environment, including business rules, exceptions, dependencies and legacy customizations. Provide senior professional expertise in the examination and definition of objectives for existing and future systems. Work with stakeholders to uncover underlying business needs, challenge existing practices, and identify opportunities to simplify, standardize or redesign processes rather than replicate the legacy environment. Partner closely with Functional Analysts and technical teams to understand system capabilities, perform fit-gap analyses, and evaluate solution options, with a preference for standard functionality and configuration over customization. Develop hands-on expertise in the assigned Banner functional area and participate directly in system configuration, functional solution design, prototyping and validation. Configure and maintain business rules, workflows and functional settings within the FBA's area of responsibility, escalating highly complex configuration or technical requirements where appropriate. Maintain an end-to-end perspective across the Student Information Systems landscape, identifying cross-functional dependencies, impacts, priorities and trade-offs. Be accountable for functional solutions within their area align with approved business requirements and intended outcomes, and for proactively identifying and escalating gaps or risks. Act as a trusted advisor and senior reference for business processes within the functional area, facilitating complex discussions and decisions across business and project teams. Provide ongoing functional ownership and stewardship for the assigned area, including complex functional support, configuration management, impact assessment of system changes and releases, and identification of opportunities to improve processes and system utilization. Serve as a senior functional escalation point for Champions, Super Users, faculties and administrative sectors. Manage the Focus Group for the functional area by facilitating user sessions, gathering feedback, and prioritizing enhancement requests from the university community. Sign off on functional designs for integrations with third-party vendors and ensure solutions align with business requirements and objectives. Remain engaged throughout the project lifecycle to ensure business requirements and intended outcomes are reflected in solution design, testing, implementation and business acceptance. Maintain requirements, key business decisions, acceptance criteria, and traceability throughout the lifecycle (gathered requirements, solution design, configuration, testing, and ultimately business acceptance). Support business data definitions, mapping, migration/conversion validation, identification of data-quality issues, and reconciliation to ensure that the data within their functional area supports the intended business processes and outcomes. Support and perform function and configuration testing, validating system behavior, business rules, workflows and end to end processes against approved design and intended business outcome.  Develop business test conditions and scenarios, support user acceptance testing, investigate function defects and work with Functional Analysts, technical teams and system integrators to validate that implemented solutions meet business needs. Actively participate in knowledge transfer and capability building with system integrator functional specialists, progressively developing deep expertise in Banner configuration, functional design, troubleshooting and administration. Apply this knowledge throughout implementation and establish the internal capability required for post-implementation functional ownership and continuous improvement. Ensure that relevant privacy, security/access, audit, records management, and institutional policy requirements are identified and incorporated into the functional solution.   Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Systems, Computer Science, Engineering or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum seven (7) years of relevant business analysis experience , preferably supporting complex business transformation or enterprise system initiatives. Demonstrated hands-on experience with ERP/SIS functional configuration, solution design, testing, troubleshooting and/or application administration.   Other Skills and Expertise: Demonstrated experience with a major ERP, Student and Finance Information System (SIS and FIS), or comparable enterprise implementation, with involvement across the full project lifecycle. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to move between strategic objectives and detailed processes, identify impacts and dependencies, and connect information across functional areas. Experience transforming complex or highly customized legacy processes into simpler, standardized future-state processes, including fit-gap analysis and evaluation of solution alternatives. Ability to quickly understand complex business processes and enterprise application capabilities and collaborate effectively with business stakeholders, Functional Analysts, and technical specialists. Strong facilitation, negotiation, and communication skills, with a demonstrated ability to challenge assumptions constructively, influence without formal authority, and guide diverse stakeholders toward decisions. Demonstrated experience working across multiple business areas, managing complex priorities, dependencies, and cross-functional decision-making. Business Analysis certification (e.g., CBAP, CCBA, PMI-PBA) and knowledge of business process modelling techniques are considered assets. Experience with Ellucian Banner or another higher education Student Information System, and/or knowledge of student administration processes, is a strong asset. Knowledge of French and English. McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require               English communication both verbally and in writing. AI fluency, including the ability to effectively and responsibly use generative AI and AI-enabled productivity tools to enhance business analysis, process discovery, requirements development, documentation, testing, research and problem-solving. Ability to critically evaluate AI-generated outputs and apply appropriate professional judgement, data privacy, security and institutional governance practices As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 5 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 07) $92,150.00 - $115,190.00 - $138,230.00 Job Profile: MPEX-IST3E - IT Business Application - Senior Professional/Manager Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Senior Director, Digital Transformation Position End Date (If applicable): 2028-01-30 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Animal-Attendant_JR0000082912": {
      "title": "Animal Attendant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Job Description – Animal Attendant Animal husbandry (55%) Assists in the proper care and maintenance of animals Feeds animals according to standards and schedules. Ensures animals have access to an adequate source of potable water Inspects animal housing conditions Cleans and changes cages, pens, enclosures, and ancillary items such as platforms, food bins, water bottles, huts, wood structures and anything inside a cage or pen for a variety of animals, accessories according to established standards and schedules Provides appropriate enrichment for different animal species (NHP toys, crinkled paper for mice, bird perches, rat tubes, etc.) …  and ensures the macro environment follows the Canadian Council on Animal Care standards (CCAC). Verifies macroenvironment - this includes visual, auditory and olfactory for anything abnormal. Verifies that the equipment is functioning normally for the individually ventilated caging system. Completes standard reports and logs for all tasks mandated by CCAC.   Animal health-related duties (8%) Monitors the general health of the animals and informs the Animal Health Technician of any changes via the rodent illness & injury reports. Reports in person or via email/phone if urgent matters arise concerning any physical and/or behavioural abnormalities, according to CMARC standards for veterinary care, following job aids. Also reports any deviations to the approved housing standards (example, overcrowding) Required to apply various treatments to animals after instructions from the Veterinary Care group (eye ointments, application of green clay over wounds, or providing wet food in a dish). Completes standard reports and logs Receiving and shipping of animals (2%) Verifies that the received animals' paperwork matches the order's paperwork Following established standards, verifies the sex, the number of animals, and the health condition of each animal and reports any discrepancies Prepares and verifies animals for shipment following standards. Shipping is usually for rodents but can also be for primates. Receiving is also rodents, but in addition can be rabbits, cats, birds, aquatic species, primates and other species that may be housed in the future. The task at the ACA level is just packing the animals in transport boxes with appropriate supplies, depending on how far they are travelling. Completes standard reports and logs Facility Maintenance (10%): Including hallways, anterooms, procedure rooms, euthanasia rooms, bathrooms in some facilities, office areas in some facilities, and lounges in some facilities. Sanitizes all animal-related areas according to standards. Reports any malfunctioning equipment or facility-related issues Performs minor work relating to the construction or repair of cages, enclosures, pens, etc. Takes inventory of animals. Assists in the inventory and restocking of animal-related supplies and Equipment Disposes of carcasses and waste according to standards Completes standard reports and logs Equipment Processing (18%) All caging, racks, accessories and enrichment. Cage Wash Sanitizes, prepares and sterilizes animal-related equipment according to standards Performs scheduled maintenance of processing equipment. Weekly and monthly maintenance of rack washers, cage washers, tunnel washers, autoclaves, dumping stations, filling stations and all associated equipment. Completes standard reports and logs   Resource Person (2%) Liaise with research staff regarding access to the equipment in the room Vet care questions that can be answered in some cases or redirected to AHTs in other cases. Demonstrate how to properly use various equipment   Demonstrate use of equipment (3%) Assist in demonstrating all duties of an animal care attendant, if required, to new employees Collaboration and support (2%) In collaboration with all team members, ensures that all tasks are accomplished on a daily and weekly basis Attends required meetings and training sessions Identifies and suggests any potential improvements to the supervisor regarding processes and/or equipment. The schedule for this position is based on a 5-day shift, including weekends This position might require the incumbent to support different areas of CMARC depending on the need.  The use of Personal Protective Equipment is mandatory (including the N95 mask).   Participation in OHP is mandatory for personnel in contact with non-human primates. Please note: This position may require work at Macdonald Campus, located in Sainte-Anne-de-Bellevue, Quebec, on an ad hoc basis. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 6 Months Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level A) $21.99 - $27.24 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Supervisor: Human Resources & Talent Management Manager Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-09 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Burnside-Hall/Multimedia-Coordinator_JR0000082930": {
      "title": "Multimedia Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Reporting to the Multimedia Services Manager, the Multimedia Coordinator oversees the day-to-day operations of an audiovisual facility, ensuring the successful delivery of high-quality live events that integrate multimedia production, audiovisual technology, staging, and digital content. The incumbent establishes project priorities and schedules, prepares quotations, and coordinates the delivery of projects and services to meet client and operational requirements. They organize, distribute, and verify the work of team members, serve as a resource person, resolve operational issues, provide guidance and support, and contribute to staff training. The incumbent also develops procedures and recommends improvements to enhance operational efficiency and support the delivery of exceptional in-person, hybrid, and virtual experiences. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Oversees the day-to-day operations of an audiovisual facility and coordinates the execution of multimedia projects and services involving audiovisual, graphic design, and photography functions. Establishes priorities, allocates resources, monitors progress, and ensures deadlines, quality standards, and client expectations are consistently met. Collaborates with internal clients and stakeholders to assess project requirements, advise on feasibility, develop time and cost estimates, and prepare quotations. Coordinates multimedia, staging, lighting, and audiovisual requirements for live, virtual, and hybrid events, including site visits, technical assessments, live video production, multi-camera direction, content playback, and on-screen graphics. Organizes, distributes and verifies the work of others, and participates in their training. Sets up, operates, and troubleshoots multimedia equipment including projection systems, LED screens, switchers, audio consoles, cameras, and streaming platforms. Ensures all technical setups meet safety, compliance, and quality standards. Participates in the development and implementation of unit procedures and work methods. Makes recommendations to improve unit efficiency including recommendations on staff requirements. Designs, modifies, builds, installs, tests, operates and maintains a variety of highly complex audio-visual systems. Reviews, tests, evaluates and modifies equipment and methodology. Develops methodology. Assesses equipment needs. Coordinates the provision of equipment. Designs or fabricates specialized equipment. Oversees equipment loans. Acts as resource person, resolves problems and instructs others. Provides technical guidance and assistance concerning work methods, the operation of a wide range of audio-visual equipment and related techniques, and the analysis of results. Keeps abreast of new developments in the field to update skills and knowledge. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Strong hands-on experience with live event technologies such as: Video switchers Audio consoles Projectors, LED walls, and media servers Streaming platforms Ability to read technical diagrams, staging layouts, and cue sheets. Detail‑oriented with strong organizational skills Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple projects simultaneously Strong troubleshooting and problem‑solving skills Well-developed communication, teamwork, and client-service skills. Valid Quebec Class 5 driver's license As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III - Multimedia 4 Years Related Experience / DEC III - Graphic Design Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level I) $35.04 - $43.42 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Creative Services Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-12 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McLennan-Library/Indigenous-Student-Ambassador_JR0000080863-1": {
      "title": "Indigenous Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the incumbent may perform some or all of the listed general administration functions. These functions are of high complexity and the incumbent performs them using precise instructions provided by their immediate supervisor or other team members. Duties and responsibilities: Act as the primary point of contact for prospective students and communities, representing McGill with cultural sensitivity and respect. Host both virtual and in-person campus tours while providing information on programs, admissions, and student life. Advise prospective Indigenous students on academic programs, admissions processes, financial aid, and specific support services with a positive and supportive attitude. Hosts and participates in virtual and in-person student panels, information sessions, cultural events and Talk with a McGill student sessions. Contribute to social media campaigns and events on platforms like Instagram, Facebook, and YouTube, and assist with video and photo editing as needed. Manage recruitment kiosks independently or with a team member during outreach events and provide written feedback for continuous improvement. Collaborate with media relations requests to share compelling stories and experiences that promote the university's culture and offerings. Conduct market research to identify target student populations and communities for focused outreach efforts, contributing to effective recruitment strategies. The list of functions outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an incumbent. Other qualifying skills: Indigenous Undergraduate student currently enrolled at McGill in Arts, Education, Engineering, Management, Music, Nursing or Science are welcome. Experience with Indigenous communities General knowledge of the downtown campus and student life. Strong written and oral communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills - must be outgoing, willing to engage and initiate conversations with students and their families / able to adapt quickly to situations (ex: construction on campus). Extremely reliable and punctual. Involvement in the McGill community (clubs, services, athletics or other university activities) an asset. Customer service and social media experience an asset. Work study applicants must provide proof of program acceptance. Hiring Unit: Admissions and Recruitment   Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $18.54 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 12 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-29 Position End Date: 2027-03-29 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-10 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Day-ChancellorHall/SAO-Law-Invigilators-Law300_JR0000082950-1": {
      "title": "SAO Law Invigilators Law300",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Job Description :  Reports to the Student Affairs Office (SAO) 45 minutes before the exam scheduled start time.  Responsible for setting up the examination room according to specific requirements as well as ensuring that equipment and facilities are functioning properly. Administers the delivery of computerized exams and documentation. Reports students’ problems to the SAO in a timely manner. Ensures that students comply with university and faculty-specific exam regulations. Responsible to report to the SAO any behavior by students or others that does not comply with university regulations. Ensures that all mobile and web-accessible electronic devices are stowed away from students prior to the start of the examination. Ensures that students are accompanied to the washroom or at any point when leaving an active examination room. Alerts the SAO when students have a question that cannot be answered by the invigilators in the examination room. At the end of the examination period, collects all exam materials and ensures nothing is left behind in the examination room(s). Responsible for returning all exams material to the SAO.    Once hired, invigilators will be asked to confirm their availability via Microsoft Form that will be circulated and will be assigned shifts 2-4 weeks prior to the start of each examination period that falls within the timing of their contract.   Mandatory Information Training Session (Virtual): Week of November 23 rd , 2026   Shifts: Exact Dates & Times TBC All Shifts will be either AM: 8:45 am to 1:30 pm or PM: 1:45 pm to 6:30pm For Fall 2026 Final Examination Period: Mondays-Fridays from December 7 - 22, 2026 For Fall 2026 Deferred Examination Period: Mondays-Fridays from February 22 - March 5, 2027 For Winter 2027 Final Examination Period: Mondays-Fridays from April 16 – 30, 2027 Qualifications Required :    Comfortable with handling computerized exams. Must be student-focused and service-oriented. Punctuality is critical. Demonstrated adequate communication and organizational skills, and the ability to transmit and receive information accurately. Demonstrated ability to listen and efficiently assist students with problems. Ability to follow instructions and to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to act in an acceptable manner so as not to disrupt students writing the exam. English, spoken and read. French an asset. Hours per week:   Variable depending on the needs of the Faculty (minimum 4 hour shift length) Description du poste : ·       Se présenter au Bureau des affaires étudiantes (BAE) 45 minutes avant l’heure prévue du début de l’examen. ·       Être responsable de la préparation de la salle d’examen conformément aux exigences spécifiques et s’assurer que l’équipement et les installations fonctionnent correctement. ·       Assurer la surveillance des examens informatisés et de la documentation connexe. ·       Signaler rapidement au BAE tout problème rencontré par les étudiants. S’assurer que les étudiants respectent les règlements de l’Université et de la Faculté relatifs aux examens. ·       Signaler au BAE tout comportement de la part des étudiants ou d’autres personnes qui ne respecte pas les règlements de l’Université. ·       S’assurer que tous les appareils électroniques mobiles et accessibles par Internet sont rangés et hors de portée des étudiants avant le début de l’examen. ·       S’assurer que les étudiants sont accompagnés lorsqu’ils se rendent aux toilettes ou lorsqu’ils quittent la salle d’examen pendant une épreuve en cours. ·       Aviser le BAE lorsqu’un étudiant pose une question à laquelle les surveillants présents dans la salle d’examen ne peuvent pas répondre. ·       À la fin de la période d’examen, recueillir tout le matériel d’examen et s’assurer que rien n’est laissé dans la ou les salles d’examen. ·       Être responsable de remettre tout le matériel d’examen au BAE.   Une fois embauchés, les surveillants devront confirmer leurs disponibilités au moyen d’un formulaire Microsoft qui leur sera transmis. Les quarts de travail seront attribués de 2 à 4 semaines avant le début de chaque période d’examens qui se déroule pendant la durée de leur contrat.   Formation obligatoire – Séance d’information (virtuelle) : Semaine du 23 novembre 2026   Quarts de travail : Dates et heures exactes à confirmer Tous les quarts de travail seront soit le matin, de 8 h 45 à 13 h 30, soit l’après-midi, de 13 h 45 à 18 h 30. ·       Pour la période des examens finaux de l’automne 2026 : o   Du lundi au vendredi, du 7 au 22 décembre 2026 ·       Pour la période des examens différés de l’automne 2026 : o   Du lundi au vendredi, du 22 février au 5 mars 2027 ·       Pour la période des examens finaux de l’hiver 2027 : o   Du lundi au vendredi, du 16 au 30 avril 2027   Qualifications requises : Être à l’aise avec la gestion des examens informatisés. Être axé sur les besoins des étudiants et offrir un service à la clientèle de qualité. La ponctualité est essentielle. Posséder de bonnes aptitudes en communication et en organisation, ainsi que la capacité de transmettre et de recevoir des renseignements avec exactitude. Démontrer une capacité d’écoute et être en mesure d’aider efficacement les étudiants à résoudre leurs problèmes. Être capable de suivre des directives et de travailler de façon autonome ainsi qu’en équipe. Être en mesure d’adopter un comportement approprié afin de ne pas perturber les étudiants pendant leur examen. Anglais parlé et lu. Le français constitue un atout.   Heures par semaine : Variables selon les besoins de la Faculté (minimum de 4 heures par quart de travail). Hourly Salary: (TSUM Invigilator) $18.00 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Grader-EDEE-253-001-004-DISE-W27_JR0000082979-1": {
      "title": "Grader EDEE 253-001/004 DISE W27",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Number and Title: EDEE 253-001/004. Kindergarten Classroom Pedagogy. Estimated Number of Grader Positions: 1 grader Total Hours of Appointment: 45 hours Hourly Rate: $17.75/hr Effective dates of grader position: Start: December 21, 2026 End: April 30, 2027 Responsibilities may include: Marking and grading. Providing feedback to students on presentations and/or coursework. Maintains records of grades by entering them into MyCourses and/or excel files. Qualifications required: Familiarity with course content. English, spoken and written. French, spoken and written, is an asset. McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $17.75 Position Start Date: 2026-12-21 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Grader-EDEE-253-002-003-DISE-W27_JR0000082978": {
      "title": "Grader EDEE 253-002/003 DISE W27",
